# Workflow Core (Fases 0 -> 6)

## Trigger
Use this rule when the user asks to work on backlog items, implementation, planning, issue creation, PR creation, or session close.

## Mandatory sequence
1. Fase 0 (bootstrap):
`./scripts/load-work-report.ps1`
2. Fase 0.5 (pre-implementation validation):
`./scripts/validate-pre-implementation.ps1`
3. Fase 1 (create issue from context when needed):
`./scripts/create-issue-from-context.ps1 -Context "<texto>"`
4. Fase 2 (implement on feature branch):
- `git checkout develop`
- `git pull origin develop`
- `git checkout -b feature/issue-<N>-<slug>`
5. Fase 3 (create PR linked to issue):
`./scripts/create-pr.ps1 -IssueNumber <N> -BranchName "feature/issue-<N>-<slug>" -CommitMessage "<msg>" -PrTitle "<title>"`
6. Fase 4 (manual review/merge in GitHub).
7. Fase 5 (post-merge mandatory close/advance):
`./scripts/advance-after-pr-close.ps1 -PullNumber <PR_NUMBER>`
8. Fase 6 (session close memory):
`./scripts/close-session.ps1 -SessionSummary "<resumen>"`

## Success criteria
- Do not claim cycle completion at PR creation time.
- Cycle is complete only after:
  - PR merged into `develop`
  - linked issue closed
  - next issue reported

## Failure criteria and handling
- If script output contains `Resultado: BLOQUEADO`, stop and report blocking reason.
- If a required script is missing, use documented `gh` fallback and explicitly report the fallback used.
